+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` validates caller-supplied `input` against the tool's declared JSON Schema `inputSchema` before invoking the executor, returning a `ToolResponse` on validation failure rather than throwing so the model can read what failed and retry within the orchestrator's tool-round budget.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` (`required`, declared types, and `enum` only, without coercing types, injecting `additionalProperties: false`, or applying defaults) before invoking the executor; when validation fails it returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing property paths and the failed constraint without calling the executor, and neither the returned text nor any emitted log line contains a rejected or identifying property value ([validated by: rejects input that violates required, type, or enum constraints without calling the executor or leaking values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L34)).
+- `ToolRegistry.register` compiles a static tool definition's `inputSchema` at registration time and throws an `Error` naming the tool when the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws at registration time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L72)).
+- A static tool definition's `inputSchema` is compiled once at registration rather than recompiled on every `execute` call.
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates `input` against the schema returned for that call rather than a stale cached one, while valid input — including unlisted extra properties — is passed through to the executor unchanged ([validated by: validates against the schema a function-valued definition returns on each call and forwards extra properties unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L83)).
+- When `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a validation failure `ToolResponse` inside `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts`, the rejection text is returned to the provider as the `tool_result` content so the model can issue a corrected call on a subsequent round within `maxToolRounds` and `processMessage` resolves ([validated by: feeds a schema rejection back through the orchestrator tool loop so the model can correct its call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L120)).
+- Calling `ToolRegistry.execute` with an unregistered tool name throws `Error('Unknown tool: <name>')` rather than returning a `ToolResponse`.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Changing the `Unknown tool: <name>` throw to a `ToolResponse`, validating tool outputs, coercing types or applying defaults, per-caller authorization, and retry, timeout, or rate limiting around tool execution.
